    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i've been looking at a lot of tech and lifestyle ads lately and there is something kinda weird about the way they talk. like, phrases like \"seamless integration,\" \"unlock your potential,\" or \"effortless experience\" appear constantly. it feels way too repetitive to be accidental. can you look into the linguistic architecture of these specific phrases? i want to see if there's a underlying structural pattern designed to bypass critical thinking or induce a certain mental state.",
